# ripgrep-only overrides: NOT read by git, and NOT read by the @-mention picker.
#
# .gitignore hides every child repo so the root tree stays clean, but ripgrep honours it too,
# which would leave root-level Grep/Glob searching only the shared layer. These negations restore
# agent-side search across the workspace; git is unaffected.
#
# @-mention autocomplete is a separate problem: the picker stops at nested .git boundaries and
# reads neither .gitignore nor .ignore (anthropics/claude-code#94991). See README.md for the
# `fileSuggestion` workaround.
#
# Add a line here when a new org repo is cloned in and gitignored. Personal checkouts: list them in
# .git/info/exclude and negate them in a local .rgignore (gitignored) instead.

!/catalog_opm/
!/cli/
!/core/
!/enhancements/
!/library/
!/modules/
!/opm/
!/opm-operator/
!/opmodel.dev/
!/opm-suite-installer/
!/.github/
